{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_801d1a7de3c9093fa3d5dc2857605f65e439d2856b962b96f5f81e603f76439d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_424d91db9f1521c36d502e6e2b9a79163e679935b94cd77215a07072a15d4067"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"rosettify-prompts is a dev-only prompt A/B/N benchmark against the Anthropic API, comparing tokens, cost, latency, and stability across concurrent conversation variants; it is not shipped to end users.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_83cd58f2a34483b2f8c557ce05f0c1d819ec98f33ba11c394c355e8823c67526","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e44560edb792003a124ae565c819e5e9ea8ec3d9eb8aa2f08215fe76b4b90342"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"The MCP server is built on FastMCP v3 with Streamable HTTP + OAuth 2.1 and STDIO transports, and the MCP pipeline involves Redis schema migrations and RAGFlow datasets.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8eade8d12226e253020c6117624af82638cf535978585b125b1f0afac9857104","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2f3c8496dd9e91320286bffb52471b9acb09bf604126103cba49ada20336bc76","slc_36c0f35f97c7f61163b4939f8beef33c807742e34b85a5be151d26ad4eddbb93"],"source_ids":["src_1ec7a16ac2d155e3a775d206dc587601"],"text":"Rosetta layers instructions at runtime — core, then organization, then project — with higher layers propagating to every project automatically, all authored in markdown and versioned in Git.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b8e736c78a091225ca6f5ec0caf31190ab3acb491641e0786abfcc237d32f060","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_193416c296e3baa92e6ec69b9aa1a32e340b09ff7bfa6e19fbfd43161f87bd46","slc_24d3201b83dc310945e09b3ebfd01b95d6bb16be3c11a350cf707cfe0dc49393"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"Rosettify is a local CLI/MCP utility providing deterministic workflow execution with zero network calls; it includes plan management, specs management, an atomic write cycle with a backup chain, and sequential phase enforcement.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c374efadca4a55f60dd11be885721d7ab3de18810307d689ba084426a5ea9374","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6c3b4eb6d064dec4581b0c699ddff442c763cd4daf1c118f47010f075d9d3b02","slc_e45bb254de82ee34969a28166a4ca1f76a6ec2758ff6bd802aef12fe4e9d3cb0"],"source_ids":["src_1ec7a16ac2d155e3a775d206dc587601"],"text":"Rosetta ships named workflows including coding-flow, requirements-authoring-flow, security-flow, testgen/api-aqa/ui-aqa flows, and code-analysis-flow, each with defined phases, subagents, and HITL gates.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c6fe0744f03e81c52accf3c047284a1720707030b557ba38f6d1e5a3bb11ea92","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ec44342d5494d11e034c222b941abf552c15609f18d389531bd6577e072f9bdc"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"The curiocity harness drives coding-agent CLIs (Claude Code, Codex) through a real PTY, reads native on-disk transcripts, auto-answers agent questions via LLM, and scores runs with deterministic checks plus an LLM judge, gating CI on the aggregate.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cd44f61b7d1232ecee8acc0671a1f022c219fbc0d9fb2936a49ef67494275bca","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b2bfed519361ca0c06389945e817cf9109511b20606fd7f2649ebd11e841e9ab","slc_bfc2b5a0dc798e6d4644291e81fc66203079ae8308e182f83903924c3a55c15e","slc_fb510ca51ce3303e547f48acbdbfd297cc2af57ddbd419fa68cc0f0bd6a4c8dd"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"Rosetta defines typed command aliases (e.g. USE SKILL, APPLY PHASE, INVOKE SUBAGENT) that work across IDEs instead of calling MCP tools directly, for portability, decoupling, and authoring.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e248fed1616b582fa63f6bcefac6f56e9cedade7d0bb0afbe22af57814afac4f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_193416c296e3baa92e6ec69b9aa1a32e340b09ff7bfa6e19fbfd43161f87bd46","slc_5f5a40bc88c7aaf775f615e010f7d74f742ef1379a614888dd2ea6e170ea17de"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"The rosettify tool is published on npm and invoked via npx, or run as a local MCP server over stdio with a --mcp flag; it offers plan and specs subcommands operating on local JSON files.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_eef3808ac163ac4403de73bf68064633c76426344aeb8884abd6190b40ae485e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2b2bf03661fc112e3d11739b8bf0f3ce7f4cc4cc4370a57c869ef722383b5a7d","slc_bfe1995422916ef0e2d21dee0f548708742f0ac03a6d54f8e74c769bb7fea5f0"],"source_ids":["src_1ec7a16ac2d155e3a775d206dc587601"],"text":"Rosetta workflows instruct the agent to delegate review to a separate subagent with a fresh context window that inspects the implementation against original specs, and to use a validator subagent with real execution evidence.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f7623ff1a657804b23de4140cfd0613403ef9063d2b6551373647c6fbb6130a1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"griddynamics/rosetta@785054e925aa snapshot 785672389caeb1f9","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d67955ebc568825154f6025880fb70bc56c39d95611d23fc50a7fdc3fea5fa8a"],"source_ids":["src_7320b6928fe75e6a8700e61610bae1b7"],"text":"The architecture follows inversion of control: Rosetta does not see or process source code; it exposes guardrails and a menu of instructions, and the coding agent selects only what it needs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:54:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5eca3e9d710942c3b03bc5647c041cda"}
